My question is when will 3.2 come out, and what will be in it?

When we were at 3.0j, there was a long list of features people 
wanted added, and a list of bugs to be fixed. ie:
  a save file for crashes
  too easy to steal from shopkeeper
  line of sight display
  ring of conflict too powerful
  polypiling too powerful
  marilith hits a long worm bug
  etc., etc.

Now most of the good suggestions I've heard of are actually in 3.1.3.
I can't really think of any major new features which nethack needs.
Sure there have been a few suggestions for new objects, and some on
limits of wishing to change the game balance, but I haven't heard of
any major features being even discussed on r.g.h.  Certainly none that
have met with widespread approval.

I'll mention a couple possibilities. Not really major new features, but 
more major than just a new item.  Let me know what you think, and also
post anything you think nethack really still needs:
  Support for races/roles:
    Instead of just picking a role (ABCEHKPRSTVW), you would pick
    a race (Human, Elf, ... (maybe Dwarf)) and a role (ABCHKPRSTVW).

  A variety of quests:
    At game start, you pick a quest.  One would be the Quest for the
    Amulet of Yendor (which would be essentially like today's nethack),
    and others might not be quite so long/tough.  Perhaps even have an
    alternate quest for the Amulet, which would be like an old version 
    of hack where it's just sitting under a boulder on level 30 or so.
  
